    "result_text": "There's a single test class, and the full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field so that `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns the upper-cased first letters of first and last name, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nChanges, each placed where the logic belongs:\n\n1. **`model/Person.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient getInitials()` computed getter. Initials derive purely from `firstName`/`lastName`, which live on `Person`, so it belongs here (and is reusable by any `Person` subtype). It mirrors the existing `getDisplayName()` derived-property pattern, with a small private `initial(...)` helper for the single-letter formatting.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema, right alongside the existing read-only `displayName`. This regenerates the `OwnerDto` with the field, and MapStruct auto-maps the matching `initials` property from the model \u2014 no mapper changes needed.\n\nBoth the new `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` and the full test suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
